00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:48.840
the same, your quality is the same, the same people are building it.

204
00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:54.240
I would still choose to build with a factory over traditional coding.

205
00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:57.000
Your mileage may vary on that.

206
00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:00.000
Personally, I like that.

207
00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:01.200
Okay, final question.

208
00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.120
Some folks may be asking should you build a software factory?

209
00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.080
Given how you all raise your hands, you already are.

210
00:11:07.080 --> 00:11:10.400
So software factory is not like a once

211
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.560
like a like rip it and then ship something new.

212
00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.800
Software factory is an incremental process where you just identify workflows,

213
00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.000
put them in a box that is legible to an agent, run it interactively

214
00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.280
a few times to build confidence and then automate it right.

215
00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.440
It's best done one workflow at a time,

216
00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:32.200
and just incrementally building towards higher

217
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:35.360
and higher levels of automation, higher and higher levels of autonomy.

218
00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:39.440
So I would argue, yeah, just how much what percent factory do

219
00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:42.480
you want to be is a better question than should I be building a factory?

