00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:44.920
Okay.

221
00:11:44.920 --> 00:11:49.680
Let's talk harness engineering, loop engineering, meta engineering.

222
00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:54.800
This as we are seeing it within Tessl, I think this is sort of becoming

223
00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:58.800
a norm across the industry is sort of the new form of

224
00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:03.120
engineering, which is instead of focusing on writing code,

225
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:08.280
instead of focusing on watching an agent write code and correct its mistakes,

226
00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:14.120
you instead focus on building and monitoring loops that are themselves

227
00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:18.000
reviewing the code, reviewing the health of your system, etc.

228
00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.280
so what do I mean by loop?

