00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:29.080
So we'll start in the center.

233
00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:32.160
You have the inner loop, which you can think of as

234
00:12:33.240 --> 00:12:36.640
the oh, I'm sorry, go ahead and take your photo.

235
00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:40.880
So the inner loop is what drives autonomy.

236
00:12:40.880 --> 00:12:45.160
This is what helps the agent actually get to the right answer on its first try.

237
00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.360
So the inner loop is the kind of stuff you're used to developing against, right?

238
00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:50.640
It's your unit tests.

239
00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:54.240
It's your linter. It is manual verification.

240
00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:58.120
Before you push up the PR, using your own eyeballs to look at the code.

241
00:12:58.120 --> 00:12:58.360
Right.

242
00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:01.680
All of these things are like relatively quick checks that are cheap.

243
00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:04.640
You're on them over and over again, and you just sort of hillclimb

